1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:09,645
A full quote for Mia Novak’s L kitchen: a mixed job with white melamine, a paint-grade MDF door, 1/4" HDF backs and 16 mm drawer boxes.

2
00:00:09,645 --> 00:00:15,890
Every price typed in this clip is an EXAMPLE price, for the demo only. Use your own supplier’s prices.

3
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:25,132
The Quote tab. Boards are priced ($825.10, the six sheets the nest buys), but edgeband, hardware and labour say "price not set".

4
00:00:25,132 --> 00:00:35,521
Never $0: an item without a price is left out, and the total says "incomplete: 9 prices not set". A quote can’t look finished when it isn’t.

5
00:00:35,521 --> 00:00:39,421
Each Configure jumps to the exact field. Start with the 1 mm white band.

6
00:00:39,421 --> 00:00:49,441
Library → Edgebands, priced per foot in an inch shop. Example price: $0.25/ft for the 1 mm ABS, $0.12/ft for the 0.4 mm PVC.

7
00:00:49,441 --> 00:00:59,850
Hardware is priced per piece, as the BOM counts it. Example prices: Salice hinge $4.50, its plate $1.50.

8
00:00:59,850 --> 00:01:03,077
A TANDEM line is one runner set per drawer, so price the set. Example price: $42 for the 18".

9
00:01:03,077 --> 00:01:15,842
The small stuff counts too. Example prices: pins $0.10, screws $0.05, dowels $0.04.

10
00:01:15,842 --> 00:01:21,131
Labour is in Settings → Pricing: a shop rate, and minutes per cabinet, drawer, door and sheet cut.

11
00:01:21,131 --> 00:01:25,139
The rate starts not set, so labour is never quoted by accident. Example price: $65 an hour.

12
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:41,747
The times are placeholders (60 / 20 / 10 / 15 min) with Configure badges. Example times for this demo: 45 min a cabinet, 15 a drawer, 8 a door, 12 a sheet.

13
00:01:41,747 --> 00:01:59,252
Back to the job’s Quote tab. Markup and sales tax are per job, both start at 0. Example: 25% markup, 6.25% sales tax.

14
00:01:59,252 --> 00:02:07,472
Tax is charged on subtotal + markup (the app says so under the field). If your state taxes materials only, adjust.

15
00:02:07,472 --> 00:02:32,723
Now the summary: board, edgeband (the BOM’s running feet incl. trim allowance), hardware, labour, subtotal, markup, tax, total.

16
00:02:32,723 --> 00:02:43,777
With these example prices: labour 8.27 h at $65, subtotal $1,753.84, 25% markup, tax on top: $2,329.32. Every line is priced, so "incomplete" is gone.

17
00:02:43,777 --> 00:02:52,371
Items lists every line: quantity, unit, each, amount. Each is rounded to the cent, so the lines add up exactly.

18
00:02:52,371 --> 00:03:06,578
Quote PDF: Letter size, job number, name and customer only, ready to send.

19
00:03:06,578 --> 00:03:23,193
BOM CSV with quote: the order list as before, then the quote block after a blank row, for your spreadsheet or accounting.

20
00:03:23,193 --> 00:03:29,917
So: prices once in the Library and Settings, markup and tax per job, and every job quotes itself. Again: all prices here were examples.
